    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'concept', 'bank', 3, 'In an allotropic study, how does the hybridization of carbon in Diamond fundamentally dictate its physical hardness compared to Graphite?', '["Diamond is heavier","Diamond''s sp³ network creates a rigid 3D structure, whereas Graphite''s sp² layers slide","Graphite has no carbon atoms","Diamond is a mixture, not an allotrope"]'::jsonb, 'B', 1, '2ccd329d92c5', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'concept', 'bank', 3, 'When a saturated solution is prepared at 80oC and then rapidly cooled to 20oC without agitation, it may become ''supersaturated.'' Why is this state thermodynamically unstable?', '["The solute concentration exceeds the equilibrium solubility limit for 20oC","The solvent evaporates","The molecules stop moving","The pressure increases"]'::jsonb, 'A', 1, '30c89d0bade1', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'concept', 'bank', 3, 'In the context of the kinetic molecular theory, why do liquids exhibit fluidity?', '["Their particles have zero kinetic energy","Their intermolecular forces are strong enough to hold volume, but weak enough to allow particle slippage","They are made of plasma","They have no mass"]'::jsonb, 'B', 1, '6b45a0fb5d61', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'concept', 'bank', 3, 'Graphite conducts electricity, while diamond does not, even though both consist entirely of carbon atoms. This difference is primarily due to:', '["Difference in purity","Difference in atomic mass","Difference in the number of carbon atoms","Difference in atomic arrangement and bonding"]'::jsonb, 'D', 1, '97660174c73b', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'concept', 'bank', 3, 'A gas occupies 500 cm³ in a container. If transferred to a 1000 cm³ container at the same temperature, the gas will:', '["Occupy 1000 cm³","Occupy 500 cm³ only","Remain at the bottom of the container","Become a liquid"]'::jsonb, 'A', 1, '321fa95ccaaa', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'scenario', 'bank', 3, 'A chemist claims that a sample is an element because it cannot be separated by chemical means. Why is this reasoning incomplete?', '["Some compounds also cannot be separated chemically.","Elements have fixed compositions.","The sample might be a mixture.","The inability to separate chemically does not alone prove it contains only one type of atom."]'::jsonb, 'D', 1, 'e0c5e173e463', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'concept', 'bank', 3, 'If all intermolecular forces in a solid were suddenly reduced to nearly zero, the solid would most likely:', '["Remain unchanged","Become more rigid","Behave like a gas","Become an element"]'::jsonb, 'C', 1, '90e0840a3e19', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'concept', 'bank', 3, 'Which of the following correctly describes the relationship between particle size and the Tyndall effect?', '["Particles must be smaller than the wavelength of light","Particles must be of a size that effectively scatters light (1-1000 nm)","Particles must be larger than 1000 nm","Particle size has no effect"]'::jsonb, 'B', 1, '5a6e3cbce56c', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'concept', 'bank', 3, 'In a suspension, the term "stationary" refers to:', '["The mixture is being heated","The state where the mixture is left undisturbed, allowing gravity to act on particles","The state where light is blocked","The state where the mixture is moving rapidly"]'::jsonb, 'B', 1, 'a3db97f49ed9', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'concept', 'bank', 3, 'When analyzing the internal structure of matter, what does the term ''intermolecular spacing'' explain about compressibility?', '["Large spacing allows particles to be pushed closer together","Small spacing prevents compression","Spacing has no relation to compressibility","Large spacing makes compression impossible"]'::jsonb, 'A', 1, '102e5d8e298f', null),
    (v_chapter, 'mcq', 'concept', 'bank', 3, 'When a solute is added to a solvent, why does the freezing point of the resulting solution often decrease?', '["Because the solution gets hotter","Because the solvent becomes a gas","Because the solute is a metal","Because the solute disrupts the crystal lattice formation of the solvent"]'::jsonb, 'D', 1, 'c59057599b03', null),
